WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:03.943
In part one

2
00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:06.813
the café's covariance matrix had

3
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:10.203
two positive eigenvalues, six and one.

4
00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:14.116
A symmetric matrix whose eigenvalues are all

5
00:00:14.203 --> 00:00:17.420
positive is called positive definite.

6
00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:20.685
Here are two symmetric matrices.

7
00:00:20.685 --> 00:00:23.235
One, K, has two minus ones.

8
00:00:23.235 --> 00:00:26.970
The other, M, has only positive entries.

9
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.523
Which one is positive definite?

10
00:00:30.523 --> 00:00:32.280
Pause and guess.

11
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.751
You can see the answer in the plane.

12
00:00:39.751 --> 00:00:41.480
For a vector x

13
00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.830
the energy is x transpose S x

14
00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:48.180
the dot product of x with S x.

15
00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:52.447
Take the café matrix C, and x equal to one

16
00:00:52.447 --> 00:00:53.449
minus one.

17
00:00:53.449 --> 00:00:55.817
C moves x to three, zero.

18
00:00:55.908 --> 00:00:58.641
The angle between them is less

19
00:00:58.732 --> 00:01:02.375
than ninety degrees, so the dot product

20
00:01:02.375 --> 00:01:05.290
the energy, is positive: three.

21
00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.096
Positive definite means this happens

22
00:01:09.192 --> 00:01:11.112
for every nonzero x

23
00:01:11.112 --> 00:01:13.800
S x always leans towards x

24
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:17.160
never ninety degrees or more away.

25
00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.838
Picture the energy as a

26
00:01:19.929 --> 00:01:21.936
height over the plane.

27
00:01:21.936 --> 00:01:23.760
For C it is a bowl

28
00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.587
with its bottom at the origin.

29
00:01:26.679 --> 00:01:29.141
Here is the curve where the

30
00:01:29.232 --> 00:01:32.060
energy equals four: an ellipse.

31
00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:34.969
Its axes are the eigenvectors.

32
00:01:34.969 --> 00:01:36.334
Along two, one

33
00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:39.832
the eigenvalue six makes the bowl steep

34
00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:41.964
so the ellipse is short.

35
00:01:41.964 --> 00:01:43.841
Along one, minus two

36
00:01:43.841 --> 00:01:46.997
the eigenvalue one makes it shallow

37
00:01:46.997 --> 00:01:49.130
and the ellipse is long.

38
00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:53.454
You do not need eigenvalues to decide.

39
00:01:53.454 --> 00:01:55.819
For a symmetric matrix

40
00:01:55.819 --> 00:01:58.479
five tests are equivalent.

41
00:01:58.479 --> 00:02:01.927
One: every eigenvalue is positive

42
00:02:01.927 --> 00:02:03.208
six and one.

43
00:02:03.208 --> 00:02:06.755
Two: every pivot is positive, five

44
00:02:06.755 --> 00:02:08.430
then six fifths.

45
00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:11.900
Three: the upper-left determinants

46
00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.396
five and six, are positive.

47
00:02:14.396 --> 00:02:17.071
Four: the energy is positive.

48
00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.923
Completing the square writes it

49
00:02:20.013 --> 00:02:22.420
with the pivots as weights.

50
00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.737
Five: C is A transpose A

51
00:02:24.737 --> 00:02:27.858
for an A with independent columns

52
00:02:27.858 --> 00:02:31.780
so the energy is the squared length of A x.

53
00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:33.827
Why do they agree?

54
00:02:33.827 --> 00:02:37.881
Write x in the perpendicular eigenvectors.

55
00:02:37.976 --> 00:02:40.616
The energy becomes six c one

56
00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:43.256
squared plus c two squared

57
00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:46.461
positive for every x exactly when

58
00:02:46.556 --> 00:02:49.290
every eigenvalue is positive.

59
00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:51.673
Back to the question.

60
00:02:51.673 --> 00:02:54.163
M has only positive entries.

61
00:02:54.163 --> 00:02:56.310
Is it positive definite?

62
00:02:56.890 --> 00:02:57.234
No.

63
00:02:57.234 --> 00:03:01.247
Its determinant is one minus nine

64
00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:02.737
minus eight.

65
00:03:02.737 --> 00:03:06.406
Take x equal to one, minus one.

66
00:03:06.406 --> 00:03:09.043
M x is minus two, two

67
00:03:09.043 --> 00:03:11.909
it points straight back.

68
00:03:11.909 --> 00:03:14.890
The energy is minus four.

69
00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:18.365
The curve of energy four is not

70
00:03:18.466 --> 00:03:22.296
an ellipse but a hyperbola: along one

71
00:03:22.296 --> 00:03:26.328
one the surface goes up, and along one

72
00:03:26.328 --> 00:03:28.747
minus one it goes down.

73
00:03:28.747 --> 00:03:30.360
It is a saddle.

74
00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:34.480
And K, with its minus ones, sends one

75
00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.746
zero to two, minus one, leaning towards x.

76
00:03:38.746 --> 00:03:42.218
Its eigenvalues are three and one

77
00:03:42.218 --> 00:03:44.202
an ellipse, a bowl.

78
00:03:44.202 --> 00:03:48.270
Never judge by the signs of the entries.

79
00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:52.279
One more case: two, four, four, eight.

80
00:03:52.279 --> 00:03:55.347
Its eigenvalues are ten and zero.

81
00:03:55.347 --> 00:03:59.408
The energy is never negative, but along two

82
00:03:59.408 --> 00:04:01.393
minus one it is zero.

83
00:04:01.483 --> 00:04:03.919
The curve of energy four is

84
00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.266
a pair of parallel lines

85
00:04:06.266 --> 00:04:08.973
the bowl has become a trough.

86
00:04:08.973 --> 00:04:11.770
That is positive semidefinite.

87
00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.947
Add a millionth of the identity

88
00:04:15.036 --> 00:04:17.598
and the trough closes into an

89
00:04:17.686 --> 00:04:19.718
extremely long ellipse.

90
00:04:19.718 --> 00:04:22.280
That trick is called jitter.

91
00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:25.725
These matrices are everywhere.

92
00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:30.117
Every A transpose A is positive semidefinite

93
00:04:30.117 --> 00:04:33.459
and so is every covariance matrix.

94
00:04:33.459 --> 00:04:35.369
For the café score

95
00:04:35.369 --> 00:04:38.711
temperature minus twice the sales

96
00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:42.435
w transpose C w is its variance: five.

97
00:04:42.435 --> 00:04:45.300
A variance is never negative.

98
00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:48.521
Gram matrices of embeddings and kernel

99
00:04:48.597 --> 00:04:50.486
matrices belong here too.

100
00:04:50.561 --> 00:04:54.037
Gaussian models need a Cholesky factorization

101
00:04:54.112 --> 00:04:56.379
which only exists for positive

102
00:04:56.454 --> 00:04:57.814
definite matrices.

103
00:04:57.814 --> 00:05:00.006
On M it stops with an error

104
00:05:00.006 --> 00:05:02.650
which makes Cholesky a quick test.

105
00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:04.200
To sum up.

106
00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:08.082
Positive definite: S x leans towards x

107
00:05:08.082 --> 00:05:10.217
the energy is a bowl

108
00:05:10.217 --> 00:05:13.614
and its level curves are ellipses.

109
00:05:13.614 --> 00:05:16.234
A saddle gives hyperbolas

110
00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:19.630
and a trough gives parallel lines.

111
00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:25.209
Eigenvalues, pivots, determinants, energy

112
00:05:25.209 --> 00:05:27.574
and A transpose A

113
00:05:27.574 --> 00:05:31.060
five faces of one property.

114
00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:34.093
Next: the energy bowl tells a

115
00:05:34.177 --> 00:05:36.038
minimum from a saddle

116
00:05:36.122 --> 00:05:38.321
and its steepness sets the

117
00:05:38.406 --> 00:05:40.520
step of gradient descent.
